  "trackFiveByFive": "5×5 Professor's Cube",
  "trackSixBySix": "6×6 cube",
  "lessonFiveIntro": "Meet the 5×5",
  "lessonFiveIntroDesc": "Fixed middles, center bars, middle edges and wings.",
  "introGoalFiveIntro": "Get to know the 5×5: fixed middles, center bars, middle edges and wings.",
  "introHowFiveIntro": "The very middle of each face never moves.\nEach edge is a middle piece with two wings.\nInner slices move pieces without touching the outside.",
  "lessonFiveCenters": "5×5 centers",
  "lessonFiveCentersDesc": "Build each center from bars of three.",
  "introGoalFiveCenters": "Build every face's 3×3 block of center pieces in one color.",
  "introHowFiveCenters": "Start from the middle piece: it tells the color.\nBuild bars of three and slide them in with an inner slice.\nFinish the last two centers together.",
  "lessonFiveEdges": "5×5 edges",
  "lessonFiveEdgesDesc": "Join two wings to their middle edge.",
  "introGoalFiveEdges": "Join each middle edge with its two wings so all 12 edges look like single pieces.",
  "introHowFiveEdges": "Match two wings to their middle edge on the front.\nTurn the inner layer, swap in an unsolved edge, turn it back.\nPair the last edges without breaking finished ones.",
  "lessonFiveSolve": "Solve the 5×5 as a 3×3",
  "lessonFiveSolveDesc": "Finish with the three crowns.",
  "introGoalFiveSolve": "Solve the reduced 5×5 like a 3×3, crown by crown.",
  "introHowFiveSolve": "Only outer turns from now on.\nFirst crown, second crown, then the yellow crown.\nThe fixed middles show each face color.",
  "lessonFiveParity": "5×5 edge parity",
  "lessonFiveParityDesc": "Fix the edge whose wings are swapped.",
  "introGoalFiveParity": "Fix the one edge whose two wings are swapped, then finish.",
  "introHowFiveParity": "It shows up as an edge that will not pair.\nPlay the long inner-slice fix once.\nEverything else returns to its place.",
  "lessonSixIntro": "Meet the 6×6",
  "lessonSixIntroDesc": "No fixed centers and four pieces in every edge.",
  "introGoalSixIntro": "Get to know the 6×6: sixteen center pieces per face and four pieces per edge.",
  "introHowSixIntro": "No center is fixed: you choose the colors as you build.\nEach edge has outer and inner wings.\nWide turns can move up to three layers.",
  "lessonSixCenters": "6×6 centers",
  "lessonSixCentersDesc": "Build 4×4 centers from bars of four.",
  "introGoalSixCenters": "Build every face's 4×4 center block in one solid color.",
  "introHowSixCenters": "Build two opposite centers first.\nMake bars of four and slide them together.\nMove single pieces with a slice, top, undo trick.",
  "lessonSixEdges": "6×6 edges",
  "lessonSixEdgesDesc": "Gather the four pieces of every edge.",
  "introGoalSixEdges": "Gather the four pieces of each edge so the 6×6 has 12 clean edges.",
  "introHowSixEdges": "Line up the outer and inner wings on the front.\nThe deep wide layer brings an edge in and out.\nFinished edges are never broken.",
  "lessonSixSolve": "Solve the 6×6 as a 3×3",
  "lessonSixSolveDesc": "Finish with the three crowns.",
  "introGoalSixSolve": "Solve the reduced 6×6 like a 3×3, crown by crown.",
  "introHowSixSolve": "Only outer turns from now on.\nThe centers you built show each face color.\nFirst crown, second crown, then the yellow crown.",
  "lessonSixParity": "6×6 parity",
  "lessonSixParityDesc": "One flipped edge or two swapped edges.",
  "introGoalSixParity": "Fix the two 6×6 cases a 3×3 never has: one flipped edge or two swapped edges.",
  "introHowSixParity": "Solve like a 3×3 until it gets stuck.\nOne flipped edge: the long parity fix.\nTwo swapped edges: the short double-turn fix.",
  "stepFivePieces": "The pieces of a 5×5",
  "stepFivePiecesBody": "The very middle piece of each face never moves, so it still tells the face's color, like on a 3×3. Around it sit eight more center pieces; each edge has a middle piece and two wings, and the corners work like a 3×3's.",
  "stepFiveSlices": "Three kinds of turns",
  "stepFiveSlicesBody": "Outer turns move one face. Wide turns move a face with the layer behind it. Inner slice turns move only a layer inside: that is how pieces change place without touching the outside.",
  "stepFiveCenterBar": "Center bars",
  "stepFiveCenterBarBody": "Build a row of three matching center pieces, then slide it next to the matching middle with an inner slice turn. Three bars make a finished center.",
  "stepFiveCenterSwap": "Swap without breaking",
  "stepFiveCenterSwapBody": "To move a single center piece: turn an inner slice, turn the top, undo the slice, turn the top back. Finished centers are restored every time.",
  "stepFiveEdgePair": "Pair wings with a middle edge",
  "stepFiveEdgePairBody": "Line up two wings beside their matching middle edge on the front, turn the inner layer down, bring in an unsolved edge from the top, then turn the inner layer back.",
  "stepFiveEdgeLast": "The last edges",
  "stepFiveEdgeLastBody": "With only a few edges left, a wide turn, a short trigger and the wide turn back pair them without breaking finished edges.",
  "stepFiveAsThree": "Now it is a 3×3",
  "stepFiveAsThreeBody": "With centers and edges done, the 5×5 behaves like a big 3×3. Use only outer turns and follow the three crowns: white cross and corners, the middle layer, then the yellow layer.",
  "stepFiveEdgeParity": "Swap the last edge's wings",
  "stepFiveEdgeParityBody": "Sometimes the last edge has its two wings swapped. A longer inner-slice algorithm swaps them back while everything else returns to its place. Then finish as a 3×3.",
  "stepSixPieces": "The pieces of a 6×6",
  "stepSixPiecesBody": "Like a 4×4, a 6×6 has no fixed center: sixteen center pieces make up each face color. Each edge has four pieces: two outer wings and two inner wings.",
  "stepSixSlices": "Turning deeper layers",
  "stepSixSlicesBody": "Wide turns can move two or three layers from a face. Inner slices on the second or third layer are the tools for centers and edges.",
  "stepSixCenterBar": "Bars of four",
  "stepSixCenterBarBody": "Build rows of four matching center pieces and slide them next to each other with inner slice turns until the face is one solid color.",
  "stepSixCenterSwap": "Move one piece at a time",
  "stepSixCenterSwapBody": "Turn the third layer, turn the top, undo, turn back: one center piece moves while finished centers come back.",
  "stepSixEdgePair": "Four pieces, one edge",
  "stepSixEdgePairBody": "Collect the four pieces of an edge on the front with the deep wide layer, then bring in an unsolved edge and turn the wide layer back.",
  "stepSixEdgeLast": "The last edges",
  "stepSixEdgeLastBody": "Pair the final edges with a short trigger between a deep wide turn and its undo, so finished edges stay paired.",
  "stepSixAsThree": "Now it is a 3×3",
  "stepSixAsThreeBody": "With 4×4 centers and paired edges, solve the 6×6 like a 3×3 with outer turns and the three crowns.",
  "stepSixOllParity": "One flipped edge",
  "stepSixOllParityBody": "If a single edge seems flipped while you solve the last layer, it is parity. Hold it at the front of the top layer and play the long fix: the first two crowns come back untouched.",
  "stepSixPllParity": "Two swapped edges",
  "stepSixPllParityBody": "If two edges look swapped at the very end, hold them at the front and back of the top layer and play the short fix of inner double turns.",
  "stageTwoFirstLayer": "Build the bottom layer",
  "stageTwoTopColor": "Make the top one color",
  "stageTwoFinish": "Finish the corners",
  "explainTwoFirstLayer": "Complete the bottom layer: its four corners match each other and the side colors.",
  "explainTwoTopColor": "Turn the top until all four top stickers show the same color, keeping the bottom layer.",
  "explainTwoFinish": "Move the last corners into place to finish the cube."
}
